  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.724989. All four (aggregation × fusion) combinations with the top encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) in multiprofile mode have been tested, and transformer+weighted is the clear winner. No untested configuration replicates this exact recipe. The closest untested variant is config_013 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted, multiprofile), which keeps the best RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion but substitutes resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l. This tests whether the image-encoder gap (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) is the dominant remaining factor or whether the transformer+weighted pipeline with resnet50 can close the gap. Based on config_001 (resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.687833, config_013 is expected to land around 0.69–0.71, unlikely to beat 0.725 but informative for cost-aware deployment. Expected relative cost: moderate, ~4–5 GPU hours (comparable to config_001 at 5.16 h, potentially slightly lower given weighted fusion was cheaper in the imagenet_vit_l comparison). As the final experiment, this is the best use of the last slot: it confirms the robustness of the winning architecture choice and provides a cheaper alternative data point without risking a large cost for a configuration (e.g., scgpt or pca variants) that is already well-established as inferior."
}

